// endpoint_set_session_remote_control.proto — SetSessionRemoteControl: turn
// the session's Remote Control bridge on or off.
//
// THE BRIDGE IS THE VENDOR'S. The vendor binary the shim drives connects the
// session to claude.ai itself (the SDK's `remote_control` control request), so
// the session runs on this machine and claude.ai, or its mobile app, attaches
// to it. Prompts typed there reach the vendor directly, past the daemon's
// submit pipeline; the shim adopts the turns they start
// (conversation.v1.PROMPT_ORIGIN_REMOTE_CONTROL).
//
// THE SETTING OUTLIVES THE VENDOR PROCESS, NOT THE SHIM. The shim holds the
// request's state and puts it in force on every vendor process it opens for the
// session from now on (a resume after a rollback or a compaction included), so
// the daemon sends it once per shim: after StartSession, and on every change.
//
// THE SAME claude.ai SESSION ACROSS SHIMS. The bridge's session id the answer
// states is the daemon's to keep; passed back as `reattach_bridge_session_id`
// on the next shim's request, it re-binds that claude.ai session rather than
// listing a new one.

